BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Autumn Afternoon (1962)
DTSTART:20261009T203000
DTEND:20261009T224500
DTSTAMP:20261009T203000Z
UID:an-autumn-afternoon-2026-10-09-20:30:00
DESCRIPTION:Yasujirō Ozu\, 1962\, Japan\, 113 min\, in Japanese with Engl
 ish subtitles\n\nThe last film by Yasujiro Ozu was also his final masterpi
 ece\, a gently heartbreaking story about a man’s dignified resignation t
 o life’s shifting currents and society’s modernization. Though the wid
 ower Shuhei (frequent Ozu leading man Chishu Ryu) has been living comforta
 bly for years with his grown daughter\, a series of events leads him to ac
 cept and encourage her marriage and departure from their home. As elegantl
 y composed and achingly tender as any of the Japanese master’s films\, A
 n Autumn Afternoon is one of cinema’s fondest farewells.\n\nSynopsis cou
 rtesy of Janus Films\n\nEstimated start: 20:50\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/
 films/an-autumn-afternoon/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
