BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seattle Film Society In Focus: Tyler Michael James (2022)
DTSTART:20261015T190000
DTEND:20261015T212000
DTSTAMP:20261015T190000Z
UID:seattle-film-society-in-focus-tyler-michael-james-2026-10-15-19:00:00
DESCRIPTION:The Seattle Film Society’s IN FOCUS showcase series returns 
 this October with a screening of Tyler Michael James’s 2022 thriller LOW
  LIFE!\n\nLOW LIFE follows Benny\, a small-time YouTube star who catches p
 redators online\, experiences a night from hell when he lets one of them i
 nto his own home.\n\nLOW LIFE will be preceded by a screening of the film
 ’s proof-of-concept short\, and a conversation about James’s film & ca
 reer will follow the screening. This event is presented in partnership wit
 h the Northwest Film Forum.\n\nThursday October 15th at the Northwest Film
  Forum. Doors at 6:30\, Film at 7. See you at the movies!\n\nEstimated sta
 rt: 19:20\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/seattle-film-society-in-focus-t
 yler-michael-james/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Staff Selects - The Daytrippers (1996)
DTSTART:20261023T173000
DTEND:20261023T192000
DTSTAMP:20261023T173000Z
UID:staff-selects-the-daytrippers-2026-10-23-17:30:00
DESCRIPTION:Greg Mottola\, 1996\, Canada\, 87 min\, in English\n\nWith its
  droll humor and bittersweet emotional heft\, the feature debut of writer-
 director Greg Mottola announced the arrival of an unassumingly sharp-witte
 d new talent on the 1990s indie film scene. When she discovers a love lett
 er written to her husband (Stanley Tucci) by an unknown paramour\, the dis
 traught Eliza (Hope Davis) turns to her tight-knit Long Island family for 
 advice. Soon the entire clan—strong-willed mom (Anne Meara)\, taciturn d
 ad (Pat McNamara)\, and jaded sister (Parker Posey) with pretentious boyfr
 iend (Liev Schreiber) in tow—has squeezed into a station wagon and heade
 d into Manhattan to find out the truth\, kicking off a one-crazy-day odyss
 ey full of unexpected detours and life-changing revelations. Performed wit
 h deadpan virtuosity by a top-flight ensemble cast\, The Daytrippers is a 
 wry and piercing look at family bonds stretched to the breaking point.\n\n
 Screening as a part of our quarterly Staff Selects series! This film was c
 hosen and presented by Camille Hermida-Fuentes\, our Director of Operation
 s! \n\nEstimated start: 17:50\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/staff-selec
 ts-the-daytrippers/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
