BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TRAUMA BOND: A Serbian Film (2026 Extended Cut) (2010)
DTSTART:20261023T200000
DTEND:20261023T220500
DTSTAMP:20261023T200000Z
UID:trauma-bond-a-serbian-film-2026-extended-cut-2026-10-23-20:00:00
DESCRIPTION:Srđan Spasojević\, 2010\, Serbia\, 104 min\, in Serbian with
  English Subtitles\n\nThis Halloween series is co-presented by Monday Mour
 ning and Scarecrow Video\, where every ticket directly benefits the world
 ’s largest physical media archive\, so no romance\, no comedy\, not even
  New French Extremity\, is lost to time. Each Trauma Bond screening featur
 es a live Drag pre-show with Miss Monday.\n\nAn aging porn star agrees to 
 participate in an “art film” in order to make a clean break from the b
 usiness\, only to discover that he has been drafted into making one of the
  harshest films ever made. In order to escape his living cinematic hell an
 d save his family’s life\, Milos will have to sacrifice everything – h
 is pride\, his morality\, his sanity\, and maybe even his own life.\n\nEst
 imated start: 20:20\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/trauma-bond-a-serbian
 -film-2026-extended-cut/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TRAUMA BOND: Come and See (1985)
DTSTART:20261009T200000
DTEND:20261009T224500
DTSTAMP:20261009T200000Z
UID:trauma-bond-come-and-see-2026-10-09-20:00:00
DESCRIPTION:Elem Klimov\, 1985\, Soviet Union\, 142 min\, in Russian and G
 erman with English Subtitles\n\nThis Halloween series is co-presented by M
 onday Mourning and Scarecrow Video\, where every ticket directly benefits 
 the world’s largest physical media archive\, so no romance\, no comedy\,
  not even New French Extremity\, is lost to time. Each Trauma Bond screeni
 ng features a live Drag pre-show with Miss Monday.\n\nThis widely acclaime
 d film from Soviet director Elem Klimov is a stunning\, senses-shattering 
 plunge into the dehumanizing horrors of war. As Nazi forces encroach on hi
 s small village in present-day Belarus\, teenage Flyora (Aleksei Kravchenk
 o\, in one of the screen’s most searing depictions of anguish since Ren
 ée Falconetti’s Joan of Arc) eagerly joins the Soviet resistance. Rathe
 r than the adventure and glory he envisioned\, what he finds is a waking n
 ightmare of unimaginable carnage and cruelty—rendered with a feverish\, 
 otherworldly intensity by Klimov’s subjective camerawork and expressioni
 stic sound design. Nearly suppressed by Soviet censors who took eight year
 s to approve its script\, Come and See is perhaps the most visceral\, impo
 ssible-to-forget antiwar film ever made.\n\nEstimated start: 20:20\n\nhttp
 s://nwfilmforum.org/films/trauma-bond-come-and-see/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TRAUMA BOND: Irreversible (2002)
DTSTART:20261016T200000
DTEND:20261016T215500
DTSTAMP:20261016T200000Z
UID:trauma-bond-irreversible-2026-10-16-20:00:00
DESCRIPTION:Gaspar Noé\, 2002\, France\, 93 min\, in English\, French\, I
 talian\, and German with English Subtitles\n\nThis Halloween series is co-
 presented by Monday Mourning and Scarecrow Video\, where every ticket dire
 ctly benefits the world’s largest physical media archive\, so no romance
 \, no comedy\, not even New French Extremity\, is lost to time. Each Traum
 a Bond screening features a live Drag pre-show with Miss Monday.\n\nOne ni
 ght. An unforgivable act. A tale told in reverse.\n\nAcclaimed filmmaker G
 aspar Noé’s unflinching exploration of human savagery and the uncomprom
 ising nature of time\, Irreversible was met with a groundswell of acclaim 
 and uproar upon its premiere at Cannes in 2002. Stylish\, sexually frank\,
  and brutal\, the film’s conceit of exploring the events of one terrible
  night on the streets of Paris in reverse chronological order was celebrat
 ed and derided in equal measure\, helping to further cement Noé’s legac
 y as a cinematic enfant terrible.\n\nEstimated start: 20:20\n\nhttps://nwf
 ilmforum.org/films/trauma-bond-irreversible/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:True Stories (1986)
DTSTART:20261007T193000
DTEND:20261007T212000
DTSTAMP:20261007T193000Z
UID:true-stories-2026-10-07-19:30:00
DESCRIPTION:David Byrne\, United States\, 1986\, 89 min\, in English\n\nTh
 ere is perhaps no film to come out of the Reagan era that is as optimistic
  and positive about American life than David Byrne’s True Stories.\n\nIn
 spired by absurd tabloid clippings he collected while on tour with Talking
  Heads with the question of “what if this was all true\,” Byrne manage
 d to create a collage of average middle-American life that elevates its su
 bjects to the extraordinary. Moving between computer chip plants\, mall fa
 shion shows\, and basement Voodou rituals\, True Stories becomes the inver
 se of a film like David Lynch’s Blue Velvet (released the same year!) in
  that it seeks to find the good hidden underneath the (sometimes) hard ext
 erior of American life deep in the heart of Texas.\n\nEstimated start: 19:
 50\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/true-stories/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:True Stories (1986)
DTSTART:20261008T190000
DTEND:20261008T205000
DTSTAMP:20261008T190000Z
UID:true-stories-2026-10-08-19:00:00
DESCRIPTION:David Byrne\, United States\, 1986\, 89 min\, in English\n\nTh
 ere is perhaps no film to come out of the Reagan era that is as optimistic
  and positive about American life than David Byrne’s True Stories.\n\nIn
 spired by absurd tabloid clippings he collected while on tour with Talking
  Heads with the question of “what if this was all true\,” Byrne manage
 d to create a collage of average middle-American life that elevates its su
 bjects to the extraordinary. Moving between computer chip plants\, mall fa
 shion shows\, and basement Voodou rituals\, True Stories becomes the inver
 se of a film like David Lynch’s Blue Velvet (released the same year!) in
  that it seeks to find the good hidden underneath the (sometimes) hard ext
 erior of American life deep in the heart of Texas.\n\nEstimated start: 19:
 20\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/true-stories/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Truth To Fiction: Cameraperson (2016)
DTSTART:20261105T193000
DTEND:20261105T213500
DTSTAMP:20261105T193000Z
UID:truth-to-fiction-cameraperson-2026-11-05-19:30:00
DESCRIPTION:Kirsten Johnson\, United States\, 2016\, 102 min\, in English
 \, Bosnian\, Farsi\, Hausa\, and Arabic with English subtitles\n\nA boxin
 g match in Brooklyn\; life in postwar Bosnia and Herzegovina\; the daily r
 outine of a Nigerian midwife\; an intimate family moment at home: these sc
 enes and others are woven into Cameraperson\, a tapestry of footage captur
 ed over the twenty-five-year career of documentary cinematographer Kirsten
  Johnson. Through a series of episodic juxtapositions\, Johnson explores t
 he relationships between image makers and their subjects\, the tension bet
 ween the objectivity and intervention of the camera\, and the complex inte
 raction of unfiltered reality and crafted narrative. A work that combines 
 documentary\, autobiography\, and ethical inquiry\, Cameraperson is both a
  moving glimpse into one filmmaker’s personal journey and a thoughtful e
 xamination of what it means to train a camera on the world.\n\nSynopsis co
 urtesy of Janus Films\n\nEstimated start: 19:50\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org
 /films/truth-to-fiction-cameraperson/
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WTF with STUFF - Holy Trinity (2019)
DTSTART:20261021T190000
DTEND:20261021T205500
DTSTAMP:20261021T190000Z
UID:wtf-with-stuff-holy-trinity-2026-10-21-19:00:00
DESCRIPTION:Glamhag\, 2019\, United States\, 91 min\, in English\n\nAfter 
 an incident huffing her drug of choice—a mysterious aerosol can from the
  ubiquitous Glamhag brand—Trinity finds herself with a newfound gift for
  speaking to the dead. Confused and more than a little curious about this 
 strange turn of events\, she seeks the counsel of a colorful cast of chara
 cters\, from priests and drag queens to a witch and more\, all of whom tea
 ch her their unique spiritual practices.\n\nAs she navigates life with thi
 s unexpected talent (and continues to huff that mysterious drug)\, Trinity
  is tossed between hallucination and reality more and more frequently\, de
 veloping a growing confidence in her strange new ability and learning to h
 arness it in surprising ways. But with any great power comes great respons
 ibility\, and soon Trinity has to decide what’s more important: her comm
 unity and personal relationships or the allure of influence and fame\n\nBo
 asting an inclusive cast (including Theo Germaine from Netflix’s The Pol
 itician) and crew comprised of diverse communities often neglected in main
 stream cinema and approaching typically taboo subjects with verve and acce
 ptance\, Holy Trinity is a sometimes raunchy\, always entertaining celebra
 tion of all that makes us different. In their feature film debut\, writer
 \, director and star Glamhag presents a vibrant and vivid portrait of frie
 ndship\, spirituality and community\, with more than a little glam sprinkl
 ed in along the way.\n\nSynopsis courtesy of Full Spectrum Films\n\nEstima
 ted start: 19:20\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/wtf-with-stuff-holy-trin
 ity/
